# Owner Decisions

This chapter records the language questions that only the project owner decides, OD1 to OD157 of
[the decision record](#owner-decisions), and how each was answered. Every one is answered:
OD1 to OD32 and OD47 on 2026-10-29, the entries OPEN-33 to OPEN-157 on 2026-10-31 and 2026-11-01
(OD94 was withdrawn: MOD-1 already refuses its case, bug 337), and the questions raised while
recording them on 2026-11-02. The entry IDs are retired and never
reused; their anchors stay, so links to them land on the answer.

The answers of 2026-10-31, 2026-11-01 and 2026-11-02 are recorded here before the rules that carry them are written.
The chapters state these decided rules now (owner revision, 2026-11-03), before being rewritten as Lean, the only normative source of the language
([ROADMAP.md](../ROADMAP.md#phases), phases B–D); until then, where a chapter still describes
the earlier behaviour, the answer below governs, and the code follows as its new-compiler slice lands.

The shape of Core was approved provisionally on 2026-11-05 ([stage A2a](#decided-2026-11-05)): it binds the design, and the owner freezes Core at stage A2c, after the four design theorems are proved against the proposed `Spec.lean` and the integration stage A2i (2026-11-06) is accepted. The project and architecture decisions are recorded here too, [below](#decided-project).

<a id="waiting-for-the-owner"></a>
## Waiting for the owner

Links only; each item's text lives where it is linked.

1. The spec read and the Core freeze, A2c ([queue](../ROADMAP.md#the-queue)).
2. The items the reviews leave open until they are fully dispositioned: SPARK review items 4(b) and
   4(c) ([SPARK review](proposals/SPARK.md)). Quantitative step and time bounds were decided on
   2026-11-07 ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-step-bounds)); the reviews' remaining disposition is unchanged.

A decided proposal moves to `docs/archive/<topic>-<date>/`.

<a id="recent-decisions"></a>
## Recent decisions

Each row records a decision and its reason. A language rule itself is its Lean definition in
[ConcreteSpec/](../ConcreteSpec/), which governs once it lands.

- The core statement ([row](#decided-project-core-statement)).
- Proof infrastructure from the first commit ([row](#decided-project-proof-infrastructure)).
- No hidden traps, and termination known beforehand ([row](#decided-project-no-hidden-traps)).
- The `checked_*`, `#[proof]` and `#[may_not_terminate]` spellings ([row](#decided-project-no-hidden-traps)).
- The per-function facts report and query ([row](#decided-project-facts-report)).
- The predictable policy ([row](#decided-project-predictable-policy)).
- Reproducible builds from slice 0 ([row](#decided-project-reproducible-builds)).
- The spec layout: one library in modules ([row](#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06)).
- A minimal root ([row](#decided-project-lean-root)).
- The LCB joins slice 0 ([row](#decided-project-proof-infrastructure)).
- Policies and declared assumptions in `Concrete.toml` ([row](#decided-project-concrete-toml)).
- `legacy/` kept until the new compiler implements a full real program such as RocksDB or ethrex ([row](#decided-project-restart)).
- OS-level sandboxing is outside the compiler's scope ([row](#decided-project-os-sandboxing)).
- Diagnostics are checker outputs ([row](#decided-project-diagnostics-2026-11-06)).
- Heap facts and memory policies ([row](#decided-project-memory-2026-11-06)).
- Secrets, noninterference and constant time ([row](#decided-project-infoflow-2026-11-06)).
- The new compiler pipeline ([row](#decided-project-pipeline-2026-11-06)).
- Thin vertical slices and their order ([row](#decided-project-vertical-slices-2026-11-06)).
- What Concrete takes from SPARK ([row](#decided-project-spark-2026-11-06)).
- Trap line, default layout and spec version ([row](#decided-project-runtime-2026-11-06)).
- The slice-0 surface: `concrete build`, `concrete facts`, unsupported-form refusals, leading zeros ([row](#decided-slice0-surface-2026-11-06)).
- The outside readers' model-first ordering ([row](#decided-project-outside-readers)).
- Step bounds: the model at slices 4–5 and proofs at slice 8 ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-step-bounds)).
- All seven showcases and their slices ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-showcases)).
- Concurrency at final slice 28, then ethlambda and the encrypted tunnel ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-final-slices)).
- Struct invariants in source at slice 17 ([revision](#decided-project-spark-2026-11-06)).
- Test runner at slice 8, formatter at 17, LSP later ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-tools)).
- Flagship and compiler speed tracking ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-performance)).
- Stack bounds from slice 0 and randomness from slice 6 ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-stack-randomness)).
- Where the decisions and their work are tracked, with a home and a gate per item ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-tracking)).
- The trusted-base statement, differential fuzzer, sanitizers, binary-size tracking and frozen JSON schema ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-early-evidence)).
- The documentation and tooling cleanup is approved, not performed by that record ([row](#decided-2026-11-07-cleanup)).

