 succeeded in 0ms:
OD1: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: the Austral model: a reference is formed by borrowing a variable or projecting through a reference; `&s.f` is sugar; a temporary is never a root; references are second-class, never stored or returned; a raw-pointer dereference needs a trusted validity premise; loans are keyed by the root variable (confirmed by OD15 (a), decided 2026-10-29)
OD2: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: (1) passing a `&mut` on is plain lending, each call's use ending when it returns, with no reborrow concept or syntax; (2) a call is refused when an exclusive argument overlaps any other argument (`h(r, r)`, `h(&mut x, &x)`, `h(&mut a, &mut a.f)` refused); as tightened by OD15 (a) the same day, two arguments that borrow the same root conflict whenever one is exclusive, so even `h(&mut a.f, &mut a.g)` is refused; (3) `&mut` refers to the place, a write through it is the write to that place at once, and copy-in/copy-out is not part of the language (only an optimization proven equivalent); (4) `defer` keeps OWN-12 and a borrow passed to a deferred call stays live until the call runs; (5) one exit sequence on every non-abort exit: the exit value, then the scope's deferred calls (last registered first, innermost scope first), then the scope's loans end, then the remaining locals are destroyed; an abort runs none of it **Canonical current root-based exclusivity rule: REF-11 and OD15(a); this historical overlap formulation is a reference to that rule.**
OD3: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: the binder is always `&T`; its mode is stored in Core; the root cannot be reassigned while a binder's loan lives. Already enforced (REF-9, PASS-2, REF-8)
OD4: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: all foreign function values are refused now; typed `extern "C" fn` types may come later
OD5: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: a bare `<T>` means Any and `T: Copy` is explicit; Copy for a generic struct or enum is declared and checked, never derived, and a generic declared Copy is Copy when every argument is
OD6: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: traits are coherent: one impl per (trait, type), the orphan rule, an ambiguous method call must be qualified, resolution by typed identity. Completed 2026-11-02: qualified as `Trait::method(&x, ...)` ([decisions](decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-audit)) **Canonical current qualification rule: this OD6 as completed by the audit below; the audit supplies syntax, not a second rule.**
OD7: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: an unsafe-module marker in source (for example `trusted mod`) never confers trust by itself, a gate lists the marked modules, and trust stays per method (OD22) **Revised 2026-11-03: this historical module-marker requirement was superseded by OD61 (2026-11-01), which removed `trusted mod`; trust and inventory remain per declaration.**
OD8: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: Austral's capability model, extended. (1) Constants only: no mutable global state of any kind (no `static mut`, no cells); a constant is truly immutable, has no interior mutability and never contains a capability, token or handle. (2) Global resources are linear tokens minted at startup: `main` receives a root resource value (in the spirit of Austral's `RootCapability`) and splits it; hardware and runtime singletons (allocator arena, UART and MMIO, panic buffer, errno, C libraries with internal state) are produced or taken only by `trusted fn` wrappers returning or taking linear tokens, and a gate lists those wrappers. (3) Tokens are ordinary values: every effect shows as a token parameter, under the existing loan and exclusivity rules (OD1, OD2, OD15), with no separate effect system. (4) Interrupt handlers, FFI callbacks and future threads get only the tokens explicitly given to them, by installation, transfer or a lock granting a borrow. (5) No life before `main`, no cleanup protocol for global state, and abort runs nothing (OD10). (6) An implicit-context mechanism, if ergonomics later demands one, is a new owner decision, never a hidden global. The cell variant was rejected after the Codex and Grok reviews (interrupts, FFI re-entrancy, linear cell contents, effect polymorphism, concurrency). Now TRUST-8 to TRUST-10 (pending, R-0557) Revised 2026-11-01 – 11-02: items 2 and 3 are superseded by the authority decision (grants handed to `main`; `with(...)` plus resource values); item 5 stands ([decisions](decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-authority))
OD9: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: one file per module with `pub` as the interface; interface artifacts generated by the compiler, no handwritten interface files; a gate diffs each module's generated interface between commits so any public-API change shows in review (R-0556)
OD10: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: integer arithmetic is checked by default; wrapping and saturating arithmetic are named operations; the shift count is checked; an abort runs no deferred call **Revised 2026-11-06 by [no hidden traps](#decided-project-no-hidden-traps): plain arithmetic is admitted only with evidence that it cannot fail; wrapping, saturating and checked (`Result`) forms cover the rest; overflow is still never silent.**
OD11: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: `as` only when lossless by value domain; every lossy conversion is a named function
OD12: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: a contract is a pure, non-consuming specification judgment, with machine and mathematical arithmetic kept distinct
OD13: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: a value moves out of raw memory only through `read_owned(p)` or an explicit replace or take through `&mut T`, and a raw address carries a trusted ownership obligation; bug 198's provisional repair is final
OD14: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: one structural well-formedness judgment runs before specialization, and function types that return a reference are refused everywhere
OD15: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner. (a) Whole-owner freezing: a live borrow of any part of a value freezes the whole owner, and loans are keyed by the root binding (REF-11 as in the current compiler); this tightens OD2's part 2: at a call, two arguments that borrow the same root conflict whenever one is exclusive, even disjoint fields (`h(&mut a.f, &mut a.g)` is refused, as in the current compiler); OD1's "keyed by the root variable" stands. (b) The strict option: the language guarantees `&mut` exclusivity, which the checker enforces (OD2, OD15a), and no compiler pass or optimization may assume or exploit it until the checker's guarantee is proven in Lean (R-0499 with the Core semantics R-0496); until then the operational loan rules are defined now, G19 included: a pointer or alias derived from a loan is valid only while that loan lives. Now REF-11@3 (partial, bug 319, which OD23 adds) and REF-14 (pending, R-0496) **Canonical current root-based exclusivity subject: REF-11 (including OD23’s re-lent case); OD2 and OD23 refer here rather than defining separate variants.**
OD16: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: refused unless parenthesized, with no exceptions; the uniform rule replaces the uppercase-name heuristic (bug 212's provisional behaviour). Now SYN-4 (pending, bug 318); whether a literal inside a call's argument list in a head counts as parenthesized is OD34
OD17: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: a field write requires a `mut` binding. Now OWN-10@2 (partial; bug 216 implements it)
OD18: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: the first matching arm in source order wins and an unreachable arm is refused; this changes the current compiler, where CoreCanonicalize moves unguarded catch-all arms to the end (bug 213's provisional behaviour)
OD19: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: the provable subset admits discarded statements, guards and ranges, each entering as its Core semantics lands (this unblocks `wip/model-coverage-3`) **Revised 2026-11-03: the guards and ranges fragments were superseded by OD55 and OD56 (2026-10-31), which removed those forms; discarded statements remain subject to the decided discard rules.**
OD20: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: std's internal `std.libc` bindings are private to std; programs cannot see them
OD21: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: only the declaring module; a newtype is constructed, and a private field read or written, only inside the module that declares it, and a parent module gets no rights over its child (TYPE-11 enforced as written)
OD22: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: trust is per method, `trusted fn` only; `trusted impl` stays refused, so bug 189's provisional repair is final
OD23: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): every argument of a call, the receiver included, is overlap-checked against the root, including re-lent `&mut` bindings, so `r.add(r.step)` is refused; read the Copy field into a `let` first. Now REF-11@3 (partial, bug 319) **Canonical current rule: REF-11 and OD15(a); this is the historical clarification of its re-lent case.**
OD24: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): `main` returns `u8` or `Unit` (exit 0); no masking, no bool mapping, no other result type. Now STMT-7@3 (partial, bug 320). Revised 2026-11-02 by the owner: `u8` only ([decisions](decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-main))
OD25: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): a bare variant name is legal only for a fieldless variant; ignoring a payload is written `Variant { .. }` or `field: _`; a struct `let` names every field or ignores one explicitly with `field: _`. Now PAT-3@3 and PAT-5@3 (partial, bug 321)
OD26: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): arithmetic, shifts and comparisons take numbers only; pointer offset, difference and ordering are `ptr::offset` and named functions. Now TYPE-6@2 (partial, bug 322)
OD27: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): `break <expr>` is refused at parse time. Now STMT-6@2 (partial, bug 323)
OD28: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): a `Destroy` bound is satisfied only by an impl; Copy types are not `Destroy` (discard them with `discard`); arrays get one written impl, or one language impl that is its own spec entry. Now TRAIT-10@2 (partial, bug 324); which array form is OD35
OD29: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): a statement expression must have type `Unit`; every other unused result needs `discard(e)`; the syntactic purity heuristic is removed. Now OWN-7@3 (partial, bug 325)
OD30: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): `e.f` requires `e` to be the struct or a reference to it; opening a `Heap` or `HeapArray` uses an explicit non-consuming place form; `*` stays the consuming move-out. Now MEM-4@3 (pending, bug 326); the place form's spelling is OD36
OD31: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): an integer literal takes its type from its context, as today; the fallback to `Int` where nothing is expected is removed, so an unconstrained literal is refused; suffixes are not required; float literals get an explicit rule under the same principle. Now ARITH-2@2 (partial, bug 327)
OD32: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner ("strict across the board"): no receiver auto-borrow: a method with `&self` or `&mut self` on an owned place is written `(&s).m()` or `(&mut s).m()`; a receiver that is already a reference is unchanged. Now OWN-15@3 (pending, bug 328)
OD33: decided 2026-10-31 by the owner's rule (every reviewer agreed, as strict as Austral or stricter): No inline `mod`; one file per module
OD34: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Only enclosing `(`/`[` parenthesize; `{` at depth 0 opens the block
OD35: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Language impl `[T; N]: Destroy` when `T: Destroy`, index order
OD36: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Only through a borrow block; no `(&h).f`
OD37: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): One trusted `ptr::diff`, ordering from its sign, no `ptr::cmp`
OD38: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Superseded by the authority decision of 2026-11-01: there is no `Root` type; `main`'s parameters are the target's singletons, hosted `fn main() with(...) -> u8` and freestanding `fn main(uart: Uart, arena: Arena) with(Device, Alloc) -> u8`; revised 2026-11-02: `main` receives the target's grants and returns `u8` only ([decisions](decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-authority))
OD39: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): `pub` decls rendered as Concrete source, compiler-generated, API-diff gate
OD40: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Moot: OD52 removed `if let`/`while let`/`let...else`
OD41: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Close as range-specific; integer matches keep a required catch-all, listing every literal is not coverage
OD42: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Keep `==`/`!=` on bool/char and `<` on char; refuse ordering on bool
OD43: decided 2026-10-31 by the owner's rule (every reviewer agreed, as strict as Austral or stricter): Refuse builtin-name collisions, publish reserved set. Completed 2026-11-02 by the owner: one namespace per module, and a child module's declarations only through `child::T` or an import ([decisions](decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-namespace))
OD44: decided 2026-10-31 by the owner's rule (every reviewer agreed, as strict as Austral or stricter): Refuse at load, naming both, until R-0440
OD45: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Bind from checked type of every argument; no result-context. **Revised by the owner 2026-11-05 (row Q5.1/Q5.4, [revision](#decided-2026-11-05-revisions)): capability arguments are written explicitly at every polymorphic call and checked; no capability inference**
OD46: decided 2026-10-31 by the owner's rule (every reviewer agreed, as strict as Austral or stricter): From checked argument types only
OD47: decided 2026-10-29 by the owner: (1) the C-style `for` is removed in every form; (2) loops are `while cond { ... }` and `for i from a until b { ... }`: half-open (`a`, ..., `b - 1`, empty when `a >= b`), the index immutable in the body, `a` and `b` evaluated once before the first iteration, the index of the bounds' integer type (both bounds of one type), `break` and `continue` as usual (`continue` advances to the next index), `from` and `until` reserved (whether reserved or contextual was reopened by the reviews of that day: OD50), LL(1) as `for` IDENT `from` expr `until` expr block with the restricted head expression for `b` (OD16); (3) in Core the counted loop desugars to the one `while` form, carrying its termination measure `b - i`. Now STMT-6@3, STMT-11@2 and STMT-12 (pending, bug 331)
OD48: decided 2026-10-31 by the owner's rule (every reviewer agreed, as strict as Austral or stricter): Refused, as OD31
OD49: decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Mathematical integer in the proof only
OD50: decided 2026-10-31 by the owner's rule (every reviewer agreed, as strict as Austral or stricter): Reserved everywhere
