legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md:34:**Rationale.** OD150 gives recorded decisions precedence until the derived grammar is resynchronized (OD77); parser implementation and the EBNF are conformance targets, not competing authorities.
legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md:279:### SYN-2. Operators group by a fixed precedence
legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md:281:**SYN-2@1.** Binary operators group left to right at the precedence levels the grammar lists before `expr`, from `||` (lowest) through `&&`, equality, comparison, `|`, `^`, `&`, shifts, `+ -` and `* / %` to `as`, and postfix operations bind tighter than prefix ones, which bind tighter than `as`.
